    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13.4">
        <head>Cn 1018 13.4</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#kennedy" n="13.4" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="76" ed="#kennedy"/>7 romfeoh be petres mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="216" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And Romfeoh be Petres mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#kennedy" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="76" ed="#kennedy"/>And Peter's Pence by St Peter's day.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="217" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And the dues to Rome are to be paid by the Feast of Saint Peter.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="335"><label>agrees with V against VI</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_11-1">V Atr 11.1</ref> <quote>the 1018 code did not number Church-scot among Church dues ... ways in which 'V' differed from 'VI' (n. 337: V Atr 11:1 ... Cn 1018 13:4–5)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:ICn_9">I Cn 9</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 9: Cn 1018 13:4  VI Atr 18</quote></note>
      </div>
    </body>
